{
 "_doc": "Reversibility lanes of the loops, graphs and gates release, and the order of evidence. classes: every action token's class (shared-types lanes.ts TOKEN_CLASS, the proxy's actions.rs token_class(), intutic_clawde actions.py TOKEN_CLASS). laneOf: the strongest class among tokens. laneHoldTokens: applicable SOPs (closedLanes, openActions, riskTier) and the workspace closedLanes to the held tokens, in class-table order. frontMatter: SOP front matter (the text between the fences) to the held tokens, through the front-matter parser (guardrailRender.ts parseFrontMatterEnforcing and sops.rs) then laneHoldTokens, and the rule errors it reports; it pins that open_actions: is read at the top level only and closed_lanes: at any indentation. classify: shell commands and every token the classifier gives them, in order (run through the shell tool `bash`), for the tokens 3.1 added: actions.rs, gate-js actions.ts and actions.py must give exactly these, and action_vectors.json carries them. holdPatterns: the snapshot rules each token's hold compiles to (lanes.ts laneHoldPatterns), and the rule ids. orderOfEvidence: the rows every decide evaluator (decideEvaluate.ts and its copies, decide_evaluate.py, the proxy's decide/gateway.rs) must keep: deterministic is the verdict of the tiers before decide (allow, refuse, or hold: a lane or revert hold not released), decide is what the decide rule would answer; outcome is the call's, and asked says whether the engine was asked at all.",
